<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>Once as prodigals we wandered,</l><l>In our folly, far from Thee;</l><l>But Thy grace, o’er sin abounding,</l><l>Rescued us from misery.</l><l>Clothed in garments of salvation</l><l>At Thy table is our place;</l><l>We rejoice, and Thou rejoicest,</l><l>In the riches of Thy grace.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>Thou the prodigal hast pardoned,</l><l>“Kissed us” with a Father’s love;</l><l>“Killed the fatted calf,” and made us</l><l>Fit Thy purpose to approve.</l><l>“It is meet,” we hear Thee saying,</l><l>“We should merry be and glad;</l><l>I have found My once-lost children,</l><l>Now they live who once were dead.”</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>“Abba, Father,” we adore Thee,</l><l>While the hosts in heaven above</l><l>E’en in us now learn the wonders</l><l>Of Thy wisdom, grace, and love.</l><l>Soon before Thy throne assembled,</l><l>All Thy children shall proclaim</l><l>Abba’s love shown in redemption,</l><l>And how full is Abba’s name!</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
